course: dictionary
lesson: 1309
title: Words that sound like their meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound like the thing they describe. Cackle is one of them: say it out loud and you can almost hear a hen. It is a verb and a noun, so you can cackle, or give a cackle. «In The Lion King the hyenas are cackling, lazy thieves, Rafiki is a wise old mandrill on the savanna, and Zazu is a hornbill who flies about reporting news.» The hyenas laugh in a loud, harsh, unpleasant way, and the words around them show they are not friendly.
explain: Read the clues around the word. Thieves steal things, and lazy means not wanting to work, so a cackle from them sounds sly or mean, not happy. Ask yourself: what kind of laugh would fit with thieves? Then put your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: Cackle has one more meaning, used in informal UK talk. If someone says «cut the cackle», they want you to stop the silly chatter and get to the point. The context tells you which meaning is right: a hen's noise, a harsh laugh, or silly talk.
fact: Cackle is a verb (to cackle) and a noun (a cackle).
fact: «Cackle» first means the loud, harsh sound a hen or goose makes.
fact: To cackle means to laugh in a loud, harsh, high way, often unpleasantly.
fact: «Cut the cackle» is informal (UK) and means stop chatting and get to the point.
fact: In stories, witches and villains often cackle when their plan works.
exercise: «In The Lion King the hyenas are cackling, lazy thieves.» What does cackling suggest about the hyenas? | They are singing a soft, sweet song | They are quietly sleeping | *They are laughing in a loud, harsh, unpleasant way | They are walking slowly home
exercise: «The hen cackled after she laid an egg.» What is the hen doing? | Eating its dinner quietly | Flying high over the farm | Running to the barn | *Making a loud, harsh sound
exercise: Mum says, «Cut the cackle and tell me what happened.» What does she want? | Go and find a hen | Start a loud, harsh laugh | *Stop the silly chatter and get to the point | Tell a long, funny story
test:
«The witch let out a cackle as her plan worked.» What is a cackle here? | A quiet hum | *A loud, harsh, high laugh | A tidy room | A clean plate
«The geese cackled at the dog.» What does cackled mean here? | Sang a sweet song | *Made a loud, harsh cry | Slept quietly in the sun | Walked slowly away
exam: «Her cackle echoed around the empty hall.» What does cackle mean here? | A quiet whisper | A kind word of thanks | *A loud, harsh, high laugh | A soft piece of cloth
